# Selection Scans Using Nucleotide Diversity, XP-CLR and FST

**Complete scripts for three window-based population-genomic scans in cucumber.**

## Overview

| Method | Ranking statistic | Candidate windows | Final processing |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Nucleotide diversity ratio | π(wild) / π(domesticated) | Highest 5% | Retain windows with ≥5 counted variants; merge touching/overlapping windows |
| XP-CLR | Raw XP-CLR score | Highest 5% | Variant-count filter, merging and gene overlap |
| FST | Weighted Weir–Cockerham FST | Highest 5% | Variant-count filter, merging and gene overlap |

All three use 20-kb windows and 2-kb steps. The 5% cutoff is an empirical ranking rule, not a significance level or FDR estimate. The scripts produce separate candidate sets; they do not calculate their intersection or a combined selection score.

**Code preservation:** the scripts below retain the supplied code, including the original column references and parameter values. Explanatory notes outside the code blocks do not modify the implementation.

## Requirements and inputs

Use Bash 4+ for associative arrays, VCFtools, BCFtools, BEDTools, the Python implementation of `xpclr` matching these options, and standard Unix text-processing tools.

| Input | Role |
| :--- | :--- |
| `Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5.imputed.vcf.gz` | π/FST calculation and XP-CLR post-filter variant counting |
| `GATK.Merged.AllChr.SNP.Filter.Miss0.5.Maf0.05.imputed.vcf.gz` | XP-CLR calculation and π/FST post-filter variant counting |
| `pop_wild.txt` | Wild sample IDs, one per line |
| `pop_dom.txt` | Domesticated sample IDs, one per line |
| `HW64.final_annotation_results.txt` | Headered tab-delimited annotation table used by XP-CLR/FST scripts |

The annotation extraction assumes chromosome, start and end are columns 2, 3 and 4, respectively, with 1-based inclusive gene coordinates. It retains the complete original rows for overlapping genes. Statistical inputs use chromosome labels such as `1`, whereas annotation overlap adds `Chr` to produce `Chr1`; adapt this rule if your naming differs.

The two VCF filenames are distinct. Confirm their reference coordinates, variant sets and filtering history. Counting variants in one file after computing statistics from the other is not automatically equivalent to counting the variants actually used in each test. Population membership is determined by the sample lists, not their filenames; record the actual accessions and group sizes.

## 1. Nucleotide diversity ratio

Save as `selection_pi.sh`.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

# Calculate genome-wide nucleotide diversity (Pi) for wild and domesticated populations
vcftools --gzvcf Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5.imputed.vcf.gz --keep pop_wild.txt --window-pi 20000 --window-pi-step 2000 --out Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5_Wild_Pi
vcftools --gzvcf Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5.imputed.vcf.gz --keep pop_dom.txt --window-pi 20000 --window-pi-step 2000 --out Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5_Dom_Pi

# Define inputs and prefix
WILD_PI="Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5_Wild_Pi.windowed.pi"
DOM_PI="Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5_Dom_Pi.windowed.pi"
VCF_FILE="GATK.Merged.AllChr.SNP.Filter.Miss0.5.Maf0.05.imputed.vcf.gz"
PREFIX="Pi_Selection"

# Match Pi windows, calculate Pi ratio (Wild/Dom), and handle zero division compactly
awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' 'NR==FNR {if(NR>1 && $6!="NaN") d[$1 FS $2 FS $3]=$6; next} FNR>1 && $6!="NaN" && (($1 FS $2 FS $3) in d) {w=$6; dom=d[$1 FS $2 FS $3]; r=(w==0&&dom==0)?0:(dom==0?w/1e-8:w/dom); print $1, $2, $3, w, dom, r}' "${DOM_PI}" "${WILD_PI}" > "${PREFIX}_Matched_Temp.txt"

echo -e "CHROM\tBIN_START\tBIN_END\tPI_WILD\tPI_DOM\tPI_RATIO" > "${PREFIX}_Matched_All.txt"
cat "${PREFIX}_Matched_Temp.txt" >> "${PREFIX}_Matched_All.txt"

# Extract top 5% Pi ratio windows
TOTAL_LINES=$(tail -n +2 "${PREFIX}_Matched_All.txt" | wc -l)
TOP5_NUM=$(awk "BEGIN {print int(${TOTAL_LINES} * 0.05)}")
echo -e "CHROM\tBIN_START\tBIN_END\tPI_WILD\tPI_DOM\tPI_RATIO" > "${PREFIX}_Top5_Regions.txt"
tail -n +2 "${PREFIX}_Matched_All.txt" | sort -k6,6nr | awk -v limit="${TOP5_NUM}" 'NR<=limit {print $0}' >> "${PREFIX}_Top5_Regions.txt"

# Convert to BED format (0-based) and retain windows with >= 5 SNPs
tail -n +2 "${PREFIX}_Top5_Regions.txt" | awk -v OFS='\t' '{print $1, $2-1, $3, $6}' > "${PREFIX}_Top5.bed"
bedtools intersect -a "${PREFIX}_Top5.bed" -b "${VCF_FILE}" -c > "${PREFIX}_Top5_SNPCount.bed"
awk '$5 >= 5' "${PREFIX}_Top5_SNPCount.bed" > "${PREFIX}_Top5_Filtered_SNP5.bed"

# Merge overlapping/adjacent windows and format final output
bedtools sort -i "${PREFIX}_Top5_Filtered_SNP5.bed" | bedtools merge -i - -d 0 -c 4,5 -o max,sum > "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged.bed"
echo -e "CHROM\tBIN_START\tBIN_END\tMAX_PI_RATIO\tTOTAL_SNPS" > "${PREFIX}_Final_Selection_Result.txt"
awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print $1, $2+1, $3, $4, $5}' "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged.bed" >> "${PREFIX}_Final_Selection_Result.txt"

# Clean up temporary files
rm "${PREFIX}_Matched_Temp.txt" "${PREFIX}_Top5.bed" "${PREFIX}_Top5_SNPCount.bed" "${PREFIX}_Top5_Filtered_SNP5.bed" "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged.bed"
```

Matched windows are joined by chromosome/start/end. The supplied zero handling is retained: both π values equal to zero gives ratio zero; a zero domesticated value with nonzero wild π uses `1e-8` as the denominator. This is a numerical convention, not an observed diversity estimate.

The script filters the top-ranked windows by variant count **after** selecting the top 5%; it does not select the top 5% anew among all count-eligible windows. No gene-overlap step is included for π in the supplied implementation.

## 2. XP-CLR

Save as `selection_xpclr.sh`. The implementation scans chromosomes in 5-Mb computational blocks, with up to 20 simultaneous processes; the statistical window is still 20 kb.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

# Define variables
VCF_GATK="GATK.Merged.AllChr.SNP.Filter.Miss0.5.Maf0.05.imputed.vcf.gz"
VCF_VAR="Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5.imputed.vcf.gz"
REF_RAW="pop_dom.txt"
REF_CLEAN="pop_dom_clean.txt"
TARGET="pop_wild.txt"
ANNO_FILE="HW64.final_annotation_results.txt"
XPCLR_OUTDIR="xpclr_results_dom.wild"
PREFIX="XPCLR_Selection"

mkdir -p "${XPCLR_OUTDIR}"

# Filter valid samples for XP-CLR
bcftools query -l "${VCF_GATK}" > vcf.samples
grep -Fxf vcf.samples "${REF_RAW}" > "${REF_CLEAN}"

# Run XP-CLR in parallel by 5Mb windows across chromosomes
declare -A chr_length=([1]=41854222 [2]=51424094 [3]=46702804 [4]=49415022 [5]=37726087 [6]=38225442 [7]=30380331)
BLOCK_SIZE=5000000
MAX_JOBS=20

for chr in {1..7}; do
    len=${chr_length[$chr]}
    for start in $(seq 1 $BLOCK_SIZE $len); do
        end=$((start + BLOCK_SIZE - 1))
        [ $end -gt $len ] && end=$len
        outfile="${XPCLR_OUTDIR}/xpclr.chr${chr}.${start}_${end}.out"

        xpclr --input "${VCF_GATK}" --samplesA "${REF_CLEAN}" --samplesB "${TARGET}" \
            --minsnps 5 --maxsnps 10000 --size 20000 --step 2000 --ld 0.95 \
            --chr "${chr}" --start "${start}" --stop "${end}" --out "${outfile}" > "${outfile}.log" 2>&1 &

        while [ $(jobs -r | wc -l) -ge $MAX_JOBS ]; do sleep 5; done
    done
done
wait

# Merge XP-CLR results
for chr in {1..7}; do
    files=$(ls ${XPCLR_OUTDIR}/xpclr.chr${chr}.*.out 2>/dev/null | sort -V)
    if [ -n "$files" ]; then
        first=$(echo $files | awk '{print $1}')
        head -n 1 "$first" > "${XPCLR_OUTDIR}/xpclr.chr${chr}.merged.txt"
        for f in $files; do tail -n +2 "$f" >> "${XPCLR_OUTDIR}/xpclr.chr${chr}.merged.txt"; done
    fi
done
awk 'FNR==1 && NR!=1 {next} {print}' ${XPCLR_OUTDIR}/xpclr.chr*.merged.txt > xpcrl.merged.txt

# Extract top 5% XP-CLR windows
VALID_LINES=$(awk -F'\t' '$12 != "" && $12 != "NaN" && NR>1' xpcrl.merged.txt | wc -l)
TOP5_NUM=$(awk "BEGIN {print int(${VALID_LINES} * 0.05)}")
awk -F'\t' '$12 != "" && $12 != "NaN" && NR>1' xpcrl.merged.txt | sort -t$'\t' -k12,12nr | awk -v limit="${TOP5_NUM}" 'NR<=limit' | \
    awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print $2, $3-1, $4, $12}' > "${PREFIX}_Top5_Temp.bed"

# Retain windows with >= 5 SNPs and merge overlapping/adjacent blocks
bedtools intersect -a "${PREFIX}_Top5_Temp.bed" -b "${VCF_VAR}" -c | awk '$5 >= 5' | bedtools sort -i - | \
    bedtools merge -i - -d 0 -c 4,5 -o max,sum > "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed"

# Format block output
echo -e "CHROM\tBLOCK_START\tBLOCK_END\tMAX_XPCLR_SCORE\tTOTAL_SNPS" > "${PREFIX}_Final_Regions.txt"
awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print $1, $2+1, $3, $4, $5}' "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed" >> "${PREFIX}_Final_Regions.txt"

# Extract candidate genes matching the regions
awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print "Chr"$1, $2, $3}' "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed" > xpclr_blocks_renamed.bed
tail -n +2 "${ANNO_FILE}" | awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print $2, $3-1, $4, $0}' > anno_temp.bed
bedtools intersect -a anno_temp.bed -b xpclr_blocks_renamed.bed -wa | sort | uniq > xpclr_intersected_genes.bed

# Format candidate gene output
head -n 1 "${ANNO_FILE}" > "${PREFIX}_Candidate_Genes.txt"
cut -f 4- xpclr_intersected_genes.bed >> "${PREFIX}_Candidate_Genes.txt"

# Clean up temporary files
rm vcf.samples "${PREFIX}_Top5_Temp.bed" "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed" xpclr_blocks_renamed.bed anno_temp.bed xpclr_intersected_genes.bed
```

### XP-CLR settings

| Setting | Supplied value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Population A | Domesticated samples retained from `pop_dom.txt` |
| Population B | `pop_wild.txt` |
| Statistical window | `20000 bp` |
| Step | `2000 bp` |
| Minimum / maximum SNPs | `5` / `10000` |
| LD setting | `0.95` |
| Computational block size | `5000000 bp` |
| Concurrent processes | Up to `20` |
| Ranked output field | Column `12`, expected raw `xpclr` |

The variable names `REF_*` and `TARGET` do not establish XP-CLR direction; the actual assignments are A = domesticated and B = wild. The developer's clarified convention identifies A as the object population and B as the reference; verify this against the exact installed implementation rather than swapping samples based on the shell variable names.

Inspect the XP-CLR header before use: this code expects chromosome/start/stop in columns 2–4 and raw score in column 12. It does not rank normalized `xpclr_norm`. The retained filename `xpcrl.merged.txt` contains the original spelling.

## 3. FST

Save as `selection_fst.sh`.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

# Calculate genome-wide FST
vcftools --gzvcf Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5.imputed.vcf.gz \
    --weir-fst-pop pop_wild.txt \
    --weir-fst-pop pop_dom.txt \
    --fst-window-size 20000 \
    --fst-window-step 2000 \
    --out Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5_Fst

# Define inputs and prefix
FST_FILE="Variants.Genome.SNP.Maf0.05Miss0.5_Fst.windowed.weir.fst"
VCF_FILE="GATK.Merged.AllChr.SNP.Filter.Miss0.5.Maf0.05.imputed.vcf.gz"
ANNO_FILE="HW64.final_annotation_results.txt"
PREFIX="FST_Selection"

# Extract top 5% FST windows
VALID_LINES=$(awk '$5 != "NaN" && NR>1' "${FST_FILE}" | wc -l)
TOP5_NUM=$(awk "BEGIN {print int(${VALID_LINES} * 0.05)}")
awk '$5 != "NaN" && NR>1' "${FST_FILE}" | sort -k5,5nr | awk -v limit="${TOP5_NUM}" 'NR<=limit' | \
    awk -v OFS='\t' '{print $1, $2-1, $3, $5}' > "${PREFIX}_Top5_Temp.bed"

# Retain windows with >= 5 SNPs
bedtools intersect -a "${PREFIX}_Top5_Temp.bed" -b "${VCF_FILE}" -c > "${PREFIX}_Top5_SNPCount.bed"
awk '$5 >= 5' "${PREFIX}_Top5_SNPCount.bed" > "${PREFIX}_Top5_Filtered.bed"

# Merge overlapping/adjacent windows and format output
bedtools sort -i "${PREFIX}_Top5_Filtered.bed" | \
    bedtools merge -i - -d 0 -c 4,5 -o max,sum > "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed"
echo -e "CHROM\tBLOCK_START\tBLOCK_END\tMAX_WEIGHTED_FST\tTOTAL_SNPS" > "${PREFIX}_Final_Regions.txt"
awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print $1, $2+1, $3, $4, $5}' "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed" >> "${PREFIX}_Final_Regions.txt"

# Extract candidate genes matching the regions
awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print "Chr"$1, $2, $3}' "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed" > fst_blocks_renamed.bed
tail -n +2 "${ANNO_FILE}" | awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{print $2, $3-1, $4, $0}' > anno_temp.bed
bedtools intersect -a anno_temp.bed -b fst_blocks_renamed.bed -wa | sort | uniq > fst_intersected_genes.bed

# Format candidate gene output
head -n 1 "${ANNO_FILE}" > "${PREFIX}_Candidate_Genes.txt"
cut -f 4- fst_intersected_genes.bed >> "${PREFIX}_Candidate_Genes.txt"

# Clean up temporary files
rm "${PREFIX}_Top5_Temp.bed" "${PREFIX}_Top5_SNPCount.bed" "${PREFIX}_Top5_Filtered.bed" "${PREFIX}_Final_Merged_Blocks.bed"
rm fst_blocks_renamed.bed anno_temp.bed fst_intersected_genes.bed
```

This code ranks column 5, expected `WEIGHTED_FST`, rather than column 6 (`MEAN_FST`). FST measures differentiation and is not directional; a high value alone does not identify which population experienced selection.

## Running the scripts

Run from a directory containing the inputs. Execute sequentially if sharing the same working directory, because XP-CLR and FST both use `anno_temp.bed`.

```bash
bash selection_pi.sh > selection_pi.log 2>&1
bash selection_xpclr.sh > selection_xpclr.log 2>&1
bash selection_fst.sh > selection_fst.log 2>&1
```

